x</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>w</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>337</mn></math>, yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative q minus w left parenthesis 19 right parenthesis equals negative 337\"><mo>-</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>337</mn></math>. Adding&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"19 w\"><mn>19</mn><mi>w</mi></math> to both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative q equals negative 337 plus 19 w\"><mo>-</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>337</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>19</mn><mi>w</mi></math>, which is equivalent to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"q equals 337 minus 19 w\"><mi>q</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>337</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn><mi>w</mi></math>. Substituting the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"left parenthesis q comma 19 right parenthesis\"><mo>(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>,</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>)</mo></math> into the second equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2 q minus w left parenthesis 19 right parenthesis equals 47\"><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>47</mn></math>. Substituting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"337 minus 19 w\"><mn>337</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn><mi>w</mi></math> in place of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"q\"><mi>q</mi></math> in the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2 q minus w left parenthesis 19 right parenthesis equals 47\"><mn>2</mn><mi>q</mi><mo>-</mo><mi>w</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>)</mo><mo>=</mo><mn>47</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"2 left parenthesis 337 minus 19 w right parenthesis minus 19 w equals 47\"><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mn>337</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>)</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>47</mn></math>. Applying the distributive property to the left-hand side of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"674 minus 38 w minus 19 w equals 47\"><mn>674</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>38</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>19</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>47</mn></math>. Combining like terms on the left-hand side of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"674 minus 57 w equals 47\"><mn>674</mn><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>57</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>47</mn></math>. Subtracting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"674\"><mn>674</mn></math> from both sides of this equation yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"minus 57 w equals negative 627\"><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>57</mn><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>627</mn></math>. Dividing both sides of this equation by <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"negative 57\"><mo>&#8722;</mo><mn>57</mn></math> yields <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\" alttext=\"w equals 11\"><mi>w</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></math>.</p>","externalid":"3265ed42-e3f1-44ac-9cb6-a8b55c776c51","correct_answer":["11"]},"createDate":1755117017717,"updateDate":1755117017717}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1755117017717, 1755117017717),
    ($SATQ$fbb0ea7f$SATQ$, $SATQ$79f6861f-e1b2-4b3a-a56b-065a572689b2$SATQ$::uuid, $SATQ$fcef72bd-6c00-44b7-ab92-642c82a48ced$SATQ$::uuid, NULL, $SATQ$qbank$SATQ$, $SATQ$SAT$SATQ$, 2, $SATQ$Math$SATQ$, $SATQ$Algebra$SATQ$, $SATQ$H$SATQ$, $SATQ$H.A.$SATQ$, $SATQ$Linear equations in one variable$SATQ$, $SATQ$E$SATQ$, 3, $SATQ$mcq$SATQ$, NULL, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">A rocket contained <math alttext="467,000"><mn>467,000</mn>
</math> kilograms (kg) of propellant before launch. Exactly <math alttext="21"><mn>21</mn>
</math> seconds after launch, <math alttext="362,105"><mn>362,105</mn>
</math> kg of this propellant remained. On average, approximately how much propellant, in kg, did the rocket burn each second after launch?</p>$SATQ$, $SATQ$[{"id":"ba70b06a-d3c8-40ba-948c-f08fddf53a7e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"4,995\"><mn>4,995</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"1ae44139-7b61-4be2-be57-f2f9a5bd5a46","content":"<p><math alttext=\"17,243\"><mn>17,243</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"838997f8-f4d7-4e13-b650-6ec98096644c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"39,481\"><mn>39,481</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3e358e11-8e79-414c-bfd2-070a2844e1be","content":"<p><math alttext=\"104,895\"><mn>104,895</mn>\n</math></p>"}]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["A"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$["ba70b06a-d3c8-40ba-948c-f08fddf53a7e"]$SATQ$::jsonb, $SATQ$<p style="text-align: left;">Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the rocket contained <math alttext="467,000 kilograms left parenthesis kg right parenthesis"><mn>467,000</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>kilograms</mtext><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>(kg)</mtext></math> of propellant before launch and had <math alttext="362,105 kg"><mn>362,105</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>kg</mtext></math> remaining exactly <math alttext="21"><mn>21</mn>
</math> seconds after launch. Finding the difference between the amount, in&nbsp;<math alttext="kg"><mtext>kg</mtext></math>, of propellant before launch and the remaining amount, in&nbsp;<math alttext="kg"><mtext>kg</mtext></math>, of propellant after launch gives the amount, in&nbsp;<math alttext="kg"><mtext>kg</mtext></math>, of propellant burned during the <math alttext="21"><mn>21</mn>
</math> seconds:&nbsp;<math alttext="467,000 minus 362,105 equals 104,895"><mn>467,000</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>362,105</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>104,895</mn></math>. Dividing the amount of propellant burned by the number of seconds yields <math alttext="StartFraction 104,895 Over 21 EndFraction equals 4,995"><mfrac><mn>104,895</mn><mn>21</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>4,995</mn></math>. Thus, an average of <math alttext="4,995 kg"><mn>4,995</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>kg</mtext></math> of propellant burned each second after launch.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice B is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice C is incorrect and may result from conceptual or calculation errors.</p>
<p style="text-align: left;">Choice D is incorrect and may result from finding the amount of propellant burned, rather than the amount of propellant burned each second.</p>$SATQ$, false, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ$manifold$SATQ$, NULL, NULL, NULL, $SATQ${"questionId":"fbb0ea7f","external_id":"79f6861f-e1b2-4b3a-a56b-065a572689b2","disclosed_item_id":null,"source":"qbank","vaultid":"fcef72bd-6c00-44b7-ab92-642c82a48ced","uId":"d862da0c-9894-4500-a18e-6f4bab074a50","program":"SAT","test_type":2,"test_type_desc":"Math","primary_class_cd":"H","domain":"Algebra","skill_cd":"H.A.","skill_desc":"Linear equations in one variable","difficulty":"E","score_band_range_cd":3,"type":"mcq","stimulus":null,"stem":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">A rocket contained <math alttext=\"467,000\"><mn>467,000</mn>\n</math> kilograms (kg) of propellant before launch. Exactly <math alttext=\"21\"><mn>21</mn>\n</math> seconds after launch, <math alttext=\"362,105\"><mn>362,105</mn>\n</math> kg of this propellant remained. On average, approximately how much propellant, in kg, did the rocket burn each second after launch?</p>","answerOptions":[{"id":"ba70b06a-d3c8-40ba-948c-f08fddf53a7e","content":"<p><math alttext=\"4,995\"><mn>4,995</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"1ae44139-7b61-4be2-be57-f2f9a5bd5a46","content":"<p><math alttext=\"17,243\"><mn>17,243</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"838997f8-f4d7-4e13-b650-6ec98096644c","content":"<p><math alttext=\"39,481\"><mn>39,481</mn>\n</math></p>"},{"id":"3e358e11-8e79-414c-bfd2-070a2844e1be","content":"<p><math alttext=\"104,895\"><mn>104,895</mn>\n</math></p>"}],"keys":["ba70b06a-d3c8-40ba-948c-f08fddf53a7e"],"correct_answer":["A"],"rationale":"<p style=\"text-align: left;\">Choice A is correct. It&rsquo;s given that the rocket contained <math alttext=\"467,000 kilograms left parenthesis kg right parenthesis\"><mn>467,000</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>kilograms</mtext><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mtext>(kg)</mtext></math> of propellant before launch and had <math alttext=\