\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fdee0fbf/img_014_1d26e9d3.png\" alt=\"y equals 74\"></span>. Since <span class=\"italic\">w</span> is the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-coordinate of this point, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"https://bkmyfcolrdumyrwktjrr.supabase.co/storage/v1/object/public/sat-images/fdee0fbf/img_015_8b859549.png\" alt=\"w equals 74\"></span>.</p>\n","answer_style":"SPR","section":"Math","image_count":16,"raw_list":{"updateDate":1691007959626,"pPcc":"SAT#H","questionId":"fdee0fbf","skill_cd":"H.C.","score_band_range_cd":6,"skill_desc":"Linear equations in two variables","createDate":1691007959626,"program":"SAT","primary_class_cd_desc":"Algebra","ibn":"029630-DC","external_id":null,"primary_class_cd":"H","uId":"3e6c99cd-5b2a-42b8-b07d-d2ce2b79a97a","difficulty":"H"},"raw_detail":{"item_id":"029630-DC","section":"Math","prompt":"<p class=\"stem_paragraph \">In the <span class=\"italic\">xy</span>-plane, line <span class=\"italic\">k</span> intersects the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-axis at the point <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"with coordinates 0 comma negative 6\"></span></span> and passes through the point <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"with coordinates 2 comma 2\"></span></span>.<span class=\"formatted_line_break delivery_mode:Both \"></span> If the point <span class=\"math_expression \"><span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"with coordinates 20 comma w \"></span></span> lies on line <span class=\"italic\">k</span>, what is the value of <span class=\"italic\">w </span>?</p>\n","answer":{"style":"SPR","rationale":"<p>The correct answer is 74. The <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-intercept of a line in the <span class=\"italic\">xy</span>-plane is the ordered pair <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"x comma y \"></span> of the point of intersection of the line with the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-axis. Since line <span class=\"italic\">k</span> intersects the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-axis at the point <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"with coordinates 0 comma negative 6\"></span>, it follows that <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the point with coordinates 0 comma negative 6 \"></span> is the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-intercept of this line. An equation of any line in the <span class=\"italic\">xy</span>-plane can be written in the form <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y equals, m x plus b\"></span>, where <span class=\"italic\">m</span> is the slope of the line and <span class=\"italic\">b</span> is the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-coordinate of the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-intercept. Therefore, the equation of line <span class=\"italic\">k</span> can be written as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y equals, m x plus negative 6\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y equals, m x minus 6\"></span>. The value of <span class=\"italic\">m</span> can be found by substituting the <span class=\"italic\">x</span>- and <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-coordinates from a point on the line, such as <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"the point with coordinates 2 comma 2\"></span>, for <span class=\"italic\">x</span> and <span class=\"italic\">y,</span> respectively. This results in <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"2 equals, 2 m minus 6\"></span>. Solving this equation for <span class=\"italic\">m</span> gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"m equals 4\"></span>. Therefore, an equation of line<span class=\"italic\"> k</span> is <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y equals, 4 x minus 6\"></span>. The value of <span class=\"italic\">w</span> can be found by substituting the <span class=\"italic\">x</span>-coordinate, 20, for <span class=\"italic\">x</span> in the equation of line <span class=\"italic\">k</span> and solving this equation for <span class=\"italic\">y.</span> This gives <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y equals, 4 times 20, minus 6\"></span>, or <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"y equals 74\"></span>. Since <span class=\"italic\">w</span> is the <span class=\"italic\">y</span>-coordinate of this point, <span class=\"math-container\"><img align=\"middle\" role=\"math\" class=\"math-img\" src=\"data:image/png;base64,\" alt=\"w equals 74\"></span>.</p>\n"}},"createDate":1691007959626,"updateDate":1691007959626,"correct_answer_extracted_from_rationale":true}$SATQ$::jsonb, 1691007959626, 1691007959626),
