s, <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x 1 comma y 1 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math> and <math alttext=\"left parenthesis x 2 comma y 2 right parenthesis\"><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced></math>, that are on the graph of <math alttext=\"y equals f left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>, and the formula <math alttext=\"m equals StartFraction y 2 minus y 1 Over x 2 minus x 1 EndFraction\"><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>x</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac></math>. Since the table shows values of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> and their corresponding values of <math alttext=\"g left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math>, substituting values of <math alttext=\"x\"><mi>x</mi>\n</math> and <math alttext=\"g left parenthesis x right parenthesis\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></math> in the equation <math alttext=\"g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals StartFraction f left parenthesis x right parenthesis Over x plus 3 EndFraction\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>f</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced></mrow><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></mfrac></math> can be used to define function <math alttext=\"f\"><mi>f</mi>\n</math>. Using the first pair of values from the table, <math alttext=\"x equals negative 27\"><mi>x</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>27</mn></math> and <math alttext=\"g left parenthesis x right parenthesis equals 3\"><mi>g</mi><mfenced><mi>x</mi></mfenced><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn></math>, yields <math alttext=\"3 equals StartFraction f left parenthesis negative 27 right parenth